    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0657" n="555" xml:id="pg555"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Carter to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-03-31"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 31,
                    1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I am sending by fast steamer to-day a copy of Sir Edward Greg’s instruction to
                    British minister at Brussels, dated 27th instant,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d532-f1"
                    /> in which he explains British Government’s view of the treaty obligations of
                    the Kongo Free State; also what, in their opinion, is required to bring the
                    administration of that State into harmony with these obligations.</p>
                <p>British minister at Brussels is directed to communicate this instruction to
                    Belgian minister for foreign affairs, after consultation with Wilson.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carter.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
